.\" index.cgi.8 - podcast feed manager FastCGI worker
.\" Dwight Spencer <denzuko@dapla.net>
.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.\"
.Dd April 14, 2026
.Dt INDEX.CGI 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm index.cgi
.Nd podcast subscription feed manager
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a FastCGI worker that provides a single-page web application for
managing a podcast subscription list stored as
.Pa feeds.xml .
It presents a browser UI through which the user can add, edit, and
remove subscriptions.
The file is read once at worker startup and written atomically on each
mutation.
.Pp
The worker is intended for single-user, local-network deployment.
It does not perform any podcast downloading or synchronisation;
that is the responsibility of a separate cron job consuming
.Pa feeds.xml .
.Pp
The UI is driven by
.Xr htmx 1
partials.
The root document is rendered once via
.Xr kcgi 3
.Fn khtml
and all subsequent partial responses are rendered via
.Fn kxml .
.Sh ROUTES
All routes are served under
.Pa /podcast/index.cgi/ .
.Bl -tag -width "POST /delete"
.It Sy GET /index
Returns the full SPA shell page.
.Xr htmx 1
loads the feed list automatically on page load.
.It Sy GET /list
Returns an HTML partial containing the current subscription cards.
.It Sy GET /add
Returns an HTML partial containing a blank add-subscription form.
.It Sy GET /edit
Returns an HTML partial containing a pre-filled edit form for the
subscription identified by the
.Va id
query parameter.
.It Sy POST /save
Creates or updates a subscription.
If the
.Va id
field is present the matching entry is updated in place; otherwise a
new entry is appended.
On success the updated list partial is returned.
On write failure the in-memory state is restored to match the on-disk
file.
.It Sy POST /delete
Soft-deletes the subscription identified by the
.Va id
query parameter,
then writes
.Pa feeds.xml
and returns the updated list partial.
.El
.Sh FORM FIELDS
The following fields are accepted by
.Sy POST /save .
All fields are required.
.Bl -tag -width "pull_time"
.It Va title
Free-form subscription name.
Maximum 256 bytes.
.It Va url
RSS feed URL.
Must begin with
.Li http://
or
.Li https:// .
Maximum 2048 bytes.
.It Va scope
Download scope.
One of:
.Bl -tag -width "latest" -compact
.It Li all
Download all available episodes.
.It Li latest
Download the most recent episode only.
.It Li none
Do not download; track the feed without fetching.
.El
.It Va day
Day of the week on which the cron job should sync this feed.
One of:
.Li Daily ,
.Li Mon ,
.Li Tue ,
.Li Wed ,
.Li Thu ,
.Li Fri ,
.Li Sat ,
.Li Sun .
.It Va pull_time
Hour of the day (24-hour clock, zero-padded) at which the cron job
should sync this feed.
One of
.Li 00
through
.Li 23 .
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "XDG_CONFIG_HOME"
.It Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
If set and non-empty, the configuration directory is
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/podcasts/ .
.It Ev HOME
If
.Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset, the configuration directory is
.Pa $HOME/.config/podcasts/ .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "$HOME/.config/podcasts/feeds.xml.tmp"
.It Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/podcasts/feeds.xml
Primary subscription database.
Read at worker startup; written atomically on save and delete
operations.
Must be a regular file; symlinks are rejected.
Maximum size 512\ KB.
.It Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/podcasts/feeds.xml.tmp
Temporary file used during atomic write.
Created alongside
.Pa feeds.xml ,
fully written, flushed, and renamed over the target.
Removed on any write or rename failure.
.It Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/podcasts/feeds.xsl
Optional XSL stylesheet reference embedded in the XML processing
instruction of the written file.
Not read or validated by
.Nm .
.El
.Sh FEEDS.XML FORMAT
The subscription file is a well-formed XML document conforming to the
following structure:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<?xml-stylesheet type="text/xsl" href="feeds.xsl"?>
<subscriptions>
  <podcast title="NAME"
           url="https://example.com/feed.rss"
           scope="latest"
           day="Daily"
           pull_time="06" />
</subscriptions>
.Ed
.Pp
Each
.Li <podcast>
element is self-closing and carries all subscription data as
attributes.
Attribute values are entity-escaped on write
.Pq Li & , Li \&" , Li < , Li >
and entity-decoded on read by the XML parser.
.Sh SANDBOXING
On supported platforms,
.Nm
calls
.Fn sandbox_lockdown_rw
after
.Pa feeds.xml
is loaded and before the FastCGI accept loop begins.
.Bl -tag -width "FreeBSD"
.It Ox
.Xr pledge 2
is used with the promises
.Li stdio unix inet wpath cpath .
.It Nx
.Xr pledge 2
is used with the same promise string
.Pq signature differs from OpenBSD .
.It Fx
.Xr cap_enter 2
is used after
.Xr cap_rights_limit 2
constrains open file descriptors.
Because capability mode forbids new
.Xr open 2
calls, the xml write path requires the file descriptor to be opened
before
.Fn sandbox_lockdown_rw
is called.
.It Linux
A
.Xr seccomp 2
BPF filter allowing only the syscalls required for FastCGI I/O and
file write is installed.
Falls back gracefully
.Pq no abort
if the kernel does not support
.Dv SECCOMP_SET_MODE_FILTER .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 on normal FastCGI loop termination and 1 on any startup
failure
.Po
configuration path unresolvable,
.Pa feeds.xml
unreadable or malformed,
sandbox initialisation failure
.Pc .
HTTP-level errors are returned as HTML partial responses within
the FastCGI loop; they do not cause process exit.
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Nm
does not log to
.Xr syslog 3 .
Errors encountered during the FastCGI loop are returned as inline
HTML error messages to the browser.
Startup failures exit silently with status 1; the FastCGI supervisor
.Po
.Xr spawn-fcgi 8 ,
.Xr nginx 8 ,
or similar
.Pc
will record the exit in its own logs.
.Sh DEPENDENCIES
.Bl -tag -width "kcgixml"
.It Xr kcgi 3
FastCGI request parsing, response framing, field validation.
.It Xr khtml 3
HTML generation for the SPA root document only.
.It Xr kxml 3
XML/HTML fragment generation for all htmx partial responses.
.It Li xml.h
mrvladus/xml.h \(em header-only XML parser and
.Li XMLString
growable buffer.
.It Li sv.h
tsoding/sv \(em string view primitives.
.It Li arena.h
Region-based allocator; all worker-lifetime allocations use the root
arena, which is destroyed on process exit.
.El
